ESP32 TOUCH SCREEN BOARD HARDWARE DESCRIPTION
––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––

The board is built around an ESP32 microcontroller.
It controls a 320x480 LCD display that uses an AXS15231B display driver.
The display communicates with the ESP32 using a QSPI interface.
QSPI uses six pins: one clock pin, one chip select pin, and four data pins.
The display also has a backlight pin that must be set high to turn the screen on.

The display pins are connected to the ESP32 as follows.
The chip select pin is connected to GPIO 45.
The clock pin is connected to GPIO 47.
The QSPI data lines are connected to GPIO 21, GPIO 48, GPIO 40, and GPIO 39.
The backlight pin is connected to GPIO 1.

To use the display in code, the Arduino GFX library is required.
The display is created using an Arduino ESP32 QSPI bus object and an AXS15231B display object.
The display must be initialised with begin, and the rotation is usually set to 2 because the screen is mounted upside down.
After initialisation, text can be drawn by setting the text color, text size, cursor position, and printing text.

The touch panel is capacitive and uses an I2C touch controller.
The touch controller communicates with the ESP32 using the I2C bus.
The SDA line is connected to GPIO 4.
The SCL line is connected to GPIO 8.
The touch controller also has an interrupt pin on GPIO 3 and a reset pin on GPIO 38.
The I2C address of the touch controller is 0x3B.

To read touch data, the ESP32 sends a specific command sequence to the touch controller over I2C.
The controller returns eight bytes of data that contain the touch state and the X and Y coordinates.
Because the display is rotated, the coordinates must be inverted by subtracting them from the screen width and height.

The backlight is controlled by GPIO 1.
Setting this pin high turns the backlight on.
Setting it low turns the backlight off.

The full pin mapping for the board is as follows.
Display chip select is on GPIO 45.
Display clock is on GPIO 47.
Display data lines are on GPIO 21, GPIO 48, GPIO 40, and GPIO 39.
Backlight is on GPIO 1.
Touch SDA is on GPIO 4.
Touch SCL is on GPIO 8.
Touch interrupt is on GPIO 3.
Touch reset is on GPIO 38.
Touch I2C address is 0x3B.

To draw text on the screen, the program clears the screen, sets the text color, sets the text size, positions the cursor, and prints the text.
To read touch input, the program calls the touch read function, which returns true if a touch is detected and outputs the X and Y coordinates.
